From 24992d05d25ec1878b4189f4259af188ee7192b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:58:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Refill worker copies an older newest-200 pickup
 truncated; hermes kanban sync refill-history

kanban_worker_node._changes_for used to import only the newest 200 task_events (EVENT_TAIL). Main
now copies the whole history (c4b8359b8f), but copies picked up before that stay truncated: a long
hub card re-picked-up by worker-1 (t_01a1ccf95e85a6f1, 17 runs, 382 events) lost its early
owner_admitted rows, so hermes-core-wt ship refused to land PR #1204: 'run N started an agent but
recorded no session'.

- kanban_pickup_history.refill fills the missing event prefix of an open foreign copy from the
  replica by uid: never invents rows, skips events whose run is not local, suppresses capture.
  Refilled rows take negative local ids below every existing id, so they sort first, are never
  'the latest X', and never cross a notifier cursor (no re-sent notifications). Safe on running cards.
- Runs on every pickup tick and on demand: hermes kanban sync refill-history [TASK_ID ...] [--json].
- Regression test: a card with >200 events keeps early-run admissions through pickup.

Verified against the real hermes-core-wt-land landing_sessions(): full and refilled copies
accepted; truncated copy and a Board-missing admission still refused.
